main thread, and only makes sense in the follower state.\n261:func (r *Raft) liveBootstrap(configuration Configuration) error {\n284:// runCandidate runs the main loop while in the candidate state.\n285:func (r *Raft) runCandidate() {\n442:func (r *Raft) setLeadershipTransferInProgress(v bool) {\n450:func (r *Raft) getLeadershipTransferInProgress() bool {\n455:func (r *Raft) setupLeaderState() {\n466:// runLeader runs the main loop while in leader state. Do the setup here and drop into\n467:// the leaderLoop for the hot loop.\n468:func (r *Raft) runLeader() {\n578:// startStopReplication will set up state and start asynchronous replication to\n579:// new peers, and stop replication to removed peers. Before removing a peer,\n580:// it'll instruct the replication routines to try to replicate to the current\n581:// index. This must only be called from the main thread.\n582:func (r *Raft) startStopReplication() {\n647:// configurationChangeChIfStable returns r.configurationChangeCh if it's safe\n648:// to process requests from it, or nil otherwise. This must only be called\n649:// from the main thread.\n651:// Note that if the conditions here were to change outside of leaderLoop to take\n652:// this from nil to non-nil, we would need leaderLoop to be kicked.\n653:func (r *Raft) configurationChangeChIfStable() chan *configurationChangeFuture {\n665:// leaderLoop is the hot loop for a leader. It is invoked\n666:// after all the various leader setup is done.\n667:func (r *Raft) leaderLoop() {\n963:// verifyLeader must be called from the main thread for safety.\n964:// Causes the followers to attempt an immediate heartbeat.\n965:func (r *Raft) verifyLeader(v *verifyFuture) {\n989:// leadershipTransfer is doing the heavy lifting for the leadership transfer.\n990:func (r *Raft) leadershipTransfer(id ServerID, address ServerAddress, repl *followerReplication, stopCh chan struct{}, doneCh chan error) {\n1032:// checkLeaderLease is used to check if we can contact a quorum of nodes\n1033:// within the last leader lease interval. If not, we need to step down,\n1034:// as we may have lost connectivity. Returns the maximum duration without\n1035:// contact. This must only be called from the main thread.\n1036:func (r *Raft) checkLeaderLease() time.Duration {\n1083:// quorumSize is used to return the quorum size. This must only be called on\n1084:// the main thread.\n1085:// TODO: revisit usage\n1086:func (r *Raft) quorumSize() int {\n1096:// restoreUserSnapshot is used to manually consume an external snapshot, such\n1097:// as if restoring from a backup. We will use the current Raft configuration,\n1098:// not the one from the snapshot, so that we can restore into a new cluster. We\n1099:// will also use the higher of the index of the snapshot, or the current index,\n1100:// and then add 1 to that, so we force a new state with a hole in the Raft log,\n1101:// so that the snapshot will be sent to followers and used for any new joiners.\n1102:// This can only be run on the leader, and returns a future that can be used to\n1103:// block until complete.\n1104:func (r *Raft) restoreUserSnapshot(meta *SnapshotMeta, reader io.Reader) error {\n1200:// appendConfigurationEntry changes the configuration and adds a new\n1201:// configuration entry to the log. This must only be called from the\n1202:// main thread.\n1203:func (r *Raft) appendConfigurationEntry(future *configurationChangeFuture) {\n1242:// dispatchLog is called on the leader to push a log to disk, mark it\n1243:// as inflight and begin replication of it.\n1244:func (r *Raft) dispatchLogs(applyLogs []*logFuture) {\n1285:// processLogs is used to apply all the committed entries that haven't been\n1286:// applied up to the given index limit.\n1287:// This can be called from both leaders and followers.\n1288:// Followers call this from AppendEntries, for n entries at a time, and always\n1289:// pass futures=nil.\n1290:// Leaders call this when entries are committed. They pass the futures from any\n1291:// inflight logs.\n1292:func (r *Raft) processLogs(index uint64, futures map[uint64]*logFuture) {\n1361:// processLog is invoked to process the application of a single committed log entry.\n1362:func (r *Raft) prepareLog(l *Log, future *logFuture) *commitTuple {\n1388:// processRPC is called to handle an incoming RPC request. This must only be\n1389:// called from the main thread.\n1390:func (r *Raft) processRPC(rpc RPC) {\n1415:// processHeartbeat is a special handler used just for heartbeat requests\n1416:// so that they can be fast-pathed if a transport supports it. This must only\n1417:// be called from the main thread.\n1418:func (r *Raft) processHeartbeat(rpc RPC) {\n1438:// appendEntries is invoked when we get an append entries RPC call. This must\n1439:// only be called from the main thread.\n1440:func (r *Raft) appendEntries(rpc RPC, a *AppendEntriesRequest) {\n1582:// processConfigurationLogEntry takes a log entry and updates the latest\n1583:// configuration if the entry results in a new configuration. This must only be\n1584:// called from the main thread, or from NewRaft() before any threads have begun.\n1585:func (r *Raft) processConfigurationLogEntry(entry *Log) error {\n1602:// requestVote is invoked when we get a request vote RPC call.\n1603:func (r *Raft) requestVote(rpc RPC, req *RequestVoteRequest) {\n1735:// requestPreVote is invoked when we get a request Pre-Vote RPC call.\n1736:func (r *Raft) requestPreVote(rpc RPC, req *RequestPreVoteRequest) {\n1810:// installSnapshot is invoked when we get a InstallSnapshot RPC call.\n1811:// We must be in the follower state for this, since it means we are\n1812:// too far behind a leader for log replay. This must only be called\n1813:// from the main thread.\n1814:func (r *Raft) installSnapshot(rpc RPC, req *InstallSnapshotRequest) {\n1955:// setLastContact is used to set the last contact time to now\n1956:func (r *Raft) setLastContact() {\n1972:// electSelf is used to send a RequestVote RPC to all peers, and vote for\n1973:// ourself. This has the side affecting of incrementing the current term. The\n1974:// response channel returned is used to wait for all the responses (including a\n1975:// vote for ourself). This must only be called from the main thread.\n1976:func (r *Raft) electSelf() <-chan *voteResult {\n2045:// preElectSelf is used to send a RequestPreVote RPC to all peers, and vote for\n2046:// ourself. This will not increment the current term. The\n2047:// response channel returned is used to wait for all the responses (including a\n2048:// vote for ourself).\n2049:// This must only be called from the main thread.\n2050:func (r *Raft) preElectSelf() <-chan *preVoteResult {\n2129:// persistVote is used to persist our vote for safety.\n2130:func (r *Raft) persistVote(term uint64, candidate []byte) error {\n2140:// setCurrentTerm is used to set the current term in a durable manner.\n2141:func (r *Raft) setCurrentTerm(t uint64) {\n2149:// setState is used to update the current state. Any state\n2150:// transition causes the known leader to be cleared. This means\n2151:// that leader should be set only after updating the state.\n2152:func (r *Raft) setState(state RaftState) {\n2161:// pickServer returns the follower that is most up to date and participating in quorum.\n2162:// Because it accesses leaderstate, it should only be called from the leaderloop.\n2163:func (r *Raft) pickServer() *Server {\n2184:// initiateLeadershipTransfer starts the leadership on the leader side, by\n2185:// sending a message to the leadershipTransferCh, to make sure it runs in the\n2186:// mainloop.\n2187:func (r *Raft) initiateLeadershipTransfer(id *ServerID, address *ServerAddress) LeadershipTransferFuture {\n2208:// timeoutNow is what happens when a server receives a TimeoutNowRequest.\n2209:func (r *Raft) timeoutNow(rpc RPC, req *TimeoutNowRequest) {\n2216:// setLatestConfiguration stores the latest configuration and updates a copy of it.\n2217:func (r *Raft) setLatestConfiguration(c Configuration, i uint64) {\n2223:// setCommittedConfiguration stores the committed configuration.\n2224:func (r *Raft) setCommittedConfiguration(c Configuration, i uint64) {\n2229:// getLatestConfiguration reads the configuration from a copy of the main\n2230:// configuration, which means it can be accessed independently from the main\n2231:// loop.\n2232:func (r *Raft) getLatestConfiguration() Configuration {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
